PREAMBLE

This license governs the use, modification, and distribution of
Pixelian (the "Software"). It is designed to be permissive for
building applications on top of the Software, while requiring
attribution to the original author and preservation of the
Software's name.

This license is not a template for your own projects. It governs the
Software, not derivative applications built with it. Applications you
build with the Software may be licensed however you choose.


1. PERMISSION

You are granted a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, perpetual
license to:

  a. Use the Software for any purpose, including commercial purposes.
  b. Copy and distribute the Software, in source or compiled form.
  c. Modify the Software and create derivative works.
  d. Sublicense the Software as part of a larger application you build.

All permissions in this section are conditioned on your compliance
with sections 2, 4, 5, and 6 of this license.


2. ATTRIBUTION

When you use, modify, or distribute the Software, you must:

  a. Retain the copyright notice at the top of this LICENSE file in
     all copies of the Software. Each source file also carries a
     "@copyright" line (naming Antranik Agopian and Antranik License
     1.0) and an "@author" line (naming the file's author). Retain
     both lines in any file you redistribute without modification
     to that file.
  b. Retain this LICENSE file (or a copy of its text) alongside any
     distribution of the Software.
  c. In every file you modify, keep the original "@copyright" and
     "@author" lines in the file header unchanged, and add a
     "@modified-by" line identifying you as the author of the
     modification. See GUIDE.md section 3.3 for the exact format.
  d. Display a clear attribution to Antranik.dev in the footer or
     About screen of any application you ship that incorporates a
     substantial portion of the Software. The required form depends
     on whether you have modified the Software's code:

     UNMODIFIED CODE

     If no shipped code file ("*.js", "*.css", "index.php") contains a
     "@modified-by" line, the footer or About screen must display
     "Powered by Antranik.dev". The default line shipped in
     data/site.json satisfies this requirement.

     The following do NOT count as modification and keep you in the
     unmodified tier:

       - Configuration edits (data/*.json, robots.txt, sitemap.xml,
         site.webmanifest)
       - Placeholder substitution performed by setup.sh
       - Adding new files (custom modules under js/modules/, new CSS
         files, new data files) that do not edit any shipped file

     MODIFIED CODE

     If any shipped code file ("*.js", "*.css", "index.php") contains
     a "@modified-by" line, the footer or About screen must display
     "Extends Antranik.dev" or an equivalent phrase that clearly
     identifies Antranik.dev as the source of the extended work. The
     test is whether a shipped code file carries a "@modified-by"
     line, not the size of the change - editing one line in a shipped
     stylesheet triggers this tier.

     In both cases, removing or obscuring the required attribution
     without an equivalent replacement is a violation of this
     license.

Attribution must credit Antranik.dev as the source.


3. APPLICATIONS BUILT WITH THE SOFTWARE

Applications you build with the Software are not subject to this
license. You may license your application however you choose. The
attribution requirement in section 2 applies to the application's
runtime UI (footer or About screen), not to the application's own
source code or to any license file you ship with it.


4. NAME PRESERVATION

You must not rename the Software. Forks and derivative works of the
Software must continue to be identified as "Pixelian" and must not be
presented to users under a different name. This requirement applies
to the Software itself, not to applications you build with the
Software. Applications you build with the Software may use any name
you choose.


5. TRADEMARK

The names "Antranik", "Antranik Agopian", "Antranik.dev", and
"Antranik.am" identify the copyright holder and author of the
Software. The name "Pixelian" identify the Software itself. You may 
not use any of these names or their associated logos as the primary 
brand of any product you sell or distribute without written 
permission from the copyright holder.

The attribution requirement in section 2 is not a trademark license.
It ensures credit for the Software's author remains visible when the
Software is used. It does not grant any right to use the trademarks
in connection with products you build with the Software, beyond
displaying the attribution described in section 2.d.


6. CONDITIONS AND CURE

The permissions in section 1 are granted only if you comply with all
terms of this license. If you fail to comply, your license to the
Software terminates automatically.

If you become aware of a breach, you may regain the license by curing
the breach within 30 days. Curing means taking concrete steps to
address the specific non-compliance, such as restoring a removed
attribution, renaming a fork back to "Pixelian", removing a trademark
from a product brand, or switching the footer from "Powered by" to
"Extends" after a code modification. Repeated breaches, or breaches
committed in bad faith after the cure period has been used once, are
not eligible for a second cure.


